<title>USA: Deere to acquire German farm machinery firm.</title>
<headline>Deere to acquire German farm machinery firm.</headline>
<dateline>MOLINE, Ill. 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deere &amp; Co said Friday it agreed to acquire the assets of the German farm machinery company, Maschinefabrik Kemper GmbH. Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The acquisition will extend Deere's position in the area of headers for use in forage harvesters.</p>
<p>Maschinefabrik Kemper produces specialized corn headers for self-propelled forage harvesters. It is based in Stadtlohn, Germany.</p>
<p>Deere manufactures a range of agricultural and construction and grounds care equipment.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
